# The fork of Idris's compiler (compiler/idris) carries the change of
# upstream/50-erased-coverage-nested-match/pull-request.diff, with the order
# of upstream/52-relevant-implicit-split: the case tree splits the
# elaborator's binding of an argument its clauses do not write after the
# patterns they do write, which fix it. Main.idr's erased `fp` and `fp3`,
# whose list index is such an argument, are covering under `%default total`;
# the pinned, unpatched Idris reports each not covering, with two missing
# cases, and refuses the module. When a re-sync brings upstream's fix, the
# report, its PINS.md entry and this test go (upstream/README.md).
. "$IDRIS_MLIR_ROOT/tests/testutils.sh"
profile_accept .
